# REST
# REST is an architecture based on resources and HTTP methods.

# Common methods:
# 1-GET
# 2-POST
# 3-PUT
# 4-DELETE

# Example:
# 1-GET /users
# 2-POST /appointments

# REST is currently the most widely used API style.

# SOAP
# SOAP is an older protocol that uses XML messaging.

# Characteristics:
# 1-Strict structure
# 2-Strong security standards
# 3-Used in enterprise environments (banks, legacy systems)

# GraphQL
# GraphQL allows the client to request exactly the data it needs.

# Example query:
# query {
#  user {
#    name
#    appointments
#  }
# }

# Advantages:
# 1-Reduces unnecessary data transfer
# 2-More efficient for complex applications

# Best Option for a Modern Startup
# For a modern startup building an online reservation system, GraphQL or REST would be the best options.
# GraphQL can be more efficient because it:
# 1-Allows precise data queries
# 2-Reduces multiple API calls
# 3-Improves performance in complex applications
# However, REST remains very popular due to its simplicity and wide adoption.
